                <pb facs="0764" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.00/595a.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the American
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In view of alarmist press telegrams, report concisely by telegraph concerning the
                    political situation, with particular reference to the return of the deposed Shah
                    and the attitude of the British and Russian Governments toward the internal
                    situation and toward the American financial advisers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
